 "marks": [
  {
   "d": "2021-11-11",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Consequently, we expect Group trading profit (EBITA (1) ) for 2021 to be in line with current analyst expectations (2) , albeit towards the lower end of the range.",
   "file": "20211111_VSVS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-03-03",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "While we remain concerned about the potential direct and indirect impacts of recent geopolitical events, which have led us to suspend our deliveries to Russian customers for the duration of hostilities, we are nevertheless confident that the Group will deliver a significant improvement in financial performance in 2022.",
   "file": "20220303_VSVS_Full-Year-Results-31-December-2021.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-05-18",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "However, despite this weakening economic environment, our expectations for the Group performance for the full year remain unchanged given the strong start to the year and our proven ability to actively manage cost pass through with pricing.",
   "file": "20220518_VSVS_AGM-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-07-25",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "Consequently, Vesuvius now expects its full year Group trading profit (EBITA)1 to be towards the top end of the range of current analysts' expectations2.",
   "file": "20220725_VSVS_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-07-28",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "This, together with the positive results of the first half, make us confident that full year Group trading profit (EBITA)(1) will be towards the top end of the range of current analysts' expectations.(2)",
   "file": "20220728_VSVS_Half-year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-11-15",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "However, due to our continuing market share gains, dynamic price management, cost reduction actions and a more gradual unwind of inventory, we now expect to deliver results somewhat above the analyst range of expectations(1) for the year to 31 December 2022.",
   "file": "20221115_VSVS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-03-02",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Accordingly, we are confident that our 2023 results will be in-line with our expectations, despite several headwinds:",
   "file": "20230302_VSVS_Final-Results-for-the-year-ended-31-December-2022.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-05-18",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Despite this, and thanks to our positive performance in the year to date, our expectations for the full year remain unchanged.",
   "file": "20230518_VSVS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-07-27",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "As a consequence, noting typical seasonality and despite remaining macro-economic uncertainties, we feel confident to modestly increase our full year expectations.",
   "file": "20230727_VSVS_Half-year-Report.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-11-14",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The resilience of our business gives us confidence that we will continue to meet our full year 2023 expectations despite weaker market conditions relative to the first half of 2023.",
   "file": "20231114_VSVS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-02-29",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Overall, on an underlying, constant currency basis (excluding one off restructuring costs estimated at £6m), we expect to make moderate progress in 2024.",
   "file": "20240229_VSVS_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-05-15",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The resilience of our business gives us continued confidence that we will deliver on our full year 2024 expectations.",
   "file": "20240515_VSVS_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
